.sp
This check is an alias of check bugprone\-unused\-return\-value \%<> with a fixed set of functions.
.sp
Suppressing issues by casting to \fBvoid\fP is enabled by default and can be
disabled by setting \fIAllowCastToVoid\fP option to \fIfalse\fP\&.
.sp
The check corresponds to a part of CERT C Coding Standard rule ERR33\-C.
Detect and handle standard library errors \%<https://\:wiki\:.sei\:.cmu\:.edu/\:confluence/\:display/\:c/\:ERR33-C\:.+Detect+and+handle+standard+library+errors>\&.
The list of checked functions is taken from the rule, with following exception:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
The check can not differentiate if a function is called with \fBNULL\fP
argument. Therefore the following functions are not checked:
\fBmblen\fP, \fBmbrlen\fP, \fBmbrtowc\fP, \fBmbtowc\fP, \fBwctomb\fP, \fBwctomb_s\fP
.UNINDENT
